  "name": "Unidad de Medida Comercial",
  "source": "UN/ECE Recommendation 20 revision 13, which is what catálogo 03 defers to — SUNAT's anexo gives only the reference, not a list. Transcribed from perunio-frontend/src/data/sunat/catalogo-06.ts (misnamed: it held catálogo 03), the longest of the copies at 41 entries. The Go pipeline had no list at all and accepted any string as a unitCode. Several codes share a wording because UN/ECE genuinely defines both — M2/MTK for metro cuadrado, M3/MTQ for metro cúbico, PR/PAR for par — so the código is what disambiguates them in a picker. KGM alone carries `gre-weight`: it is the only unidad the GRE validator accepts for a guía's peso bruto.",
